{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "the-architecture-consultation-gate-fires-on-architectureimpa",
  "title": "The architecture consultation gate fires on architectureImpact, not on the derived change class",
  "requirement": "REQ-308, corrected reading: delegate_task refuses a delegation that declares architectureImpact until the Analysis Record holds an ARCH- decision in decisions[], whatever changeClass it names - L2, L1, or none; a delegation without the flag is unaffected whatever its class. A change class must not be the trigger, because the record answers \"L1\" when the class is omitted.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "plugins/orchestrator/test/architect-consult-gate.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test plugins/orchestrator/test/architect-consult-gate.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Mount the orchestrator with a fake board and an analysis service whose gate answers \"L1\" for an omitted changeClass, as plugins/analysis/store.mjs does (effective = klass ?? \"L1\").",
    "delegate_task with changeClass L2, architectureImpact true and decisions[] with no ARCH- entry: refused, no task row, no child.",
    "delegate_task with architectureImpact true and no changeClass: refused with the same code.",
    "delegate_task with changeClass L1 and architectureImpact true: refused with the same code.",
    "delegate_task with the flag and decisions[] carrying {id:\"ARCH-1\"}: one task row, one child.",
    "delegate_task for L0, L1 and L2 without the flag: still pass.",
    "Read the workspace Analysis Record through the real store on two copies: one without an ARCH- decision (refused) and one with it (passed)."
  ],
  "expected": "delegate_task returns {ok:false, code:\"architect_consult_required\"} with a message naming decisions[] and ARCH-, writing no task row and starting no child, for changeClass L2 with the flag, for the flag with no changeClass and for changeClass L1 with the flag; the same flagged delegation passes once decisions[] carries an ARCH- entry; L0, L1 and L2 without the flag pass unchanged; the real Analysis Record read by the real store refuses without an ARCH- decision and passes with one.",
  "tags": [
    "orchestrator",
    "delegate_task",
    "DEC-002",
    "architect",
    "gate",
    "architectureImpact"
  ],
